<%# scope: :project — WITHOUT it, form_with derives the param key from the model class, and a
    NAMESPACED model (Maker::Project) yields `maker_project[...]`, which ProjectsController's
    params.require(:project) rejects → every create/edit through the form silently fails. %>
<%= form_with model: project, scope: :project,
              url: (project.persisted? ? project_path(project) : projects_path),
              method: (project.persisted? ? :patch : :post), class: "project-form" do |f| %>
  <% if project.errors.any? %>
    <div class="form-errors flash-alert">
      <%= project.errors.full_messages.to_sentence %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <label class="field">
    <span>Name</span>
    <%= f.text_field :name, required: true, autofocus: true %>
  </label>

  <label class="field">
    <span>Description</span>
    <%= f.text_area :description, rows: 5, placeholder: "What are you building?" %>
  </label>

  <label class="field">
    <span>Tags</span>
    <%= f.text_field :tag_list, value: project.tag_list, placeholder: "laser, firmware" %>
    <span class="field-hint muted">Comma-separated</span>
  </label>

  <%# VISIBILITY AND LICENCE MOVED TO THE PUBLISH PANEL (stage 4, S4-4), on the project page, where
      the three states can carry their meanings and a handle can be claimed inline. They are not
      duplicated here: one column with two controls is the shape §14a keeps recording, and
      `project_params` still permits both because the panel posts to this same #update. %>

  <%#
    THE COVER IMAGE, choosable here rather than only inferred. `Maker::Project#cover_node_id` falls
    back to the derived pick (first image, else first model, else first attachment) whenever the
    column is blank, so a project nobody has chosen one for looks exactly as it always did — this
    field only makes the choice expressible.

    THE EXISTING CHOOSER IN FILE MODE, NOT A NEW PICKER. `shared/_folder_field` + the `filechooser`
    controller already do native-OS Miller-columns browsing and have supported `mode: "file"` since
    they were written; this is the first caller to use it. Browsing the LIBRARY rather than the
    project's own attachments is deliberate and is what makes the field work on `new`, where the
    project has no attachments yet — and an image you are about to attach is already in the library
    either way.

    `project[:cover_node_id]`, NOT `project.cover_node_id`: the reader is overridden to fall back to
    the DERIVED pick, so the method would pre-fill this field with a file the user never chose,
    turning "no choice yet" into an explicit choice the moment they saved anything else on the form.
  %>
  <% chosen = project[:cover_node_id].presence %>
  <% chosen_node = chosen && current_user.nodes.present.find_by(node_id: chosen, kind: "file") %>
  <div class="field">
    <span>Cover image</span>
    <%= render "shared/folder_field",
               name: "project[cover_node_id]",
               mode: "file",
               children_url: library_children_path,
               create_url: library_folders_path,
               value: chosen,
               root_label: "Choose automatically",
               label: (chosen_node&.name || "Choose automatically") %>
    <%#
      THE WAY BACK. Without it, choosing a cover is a one-way door — there would be no value the
      chooser can produce that means "none", so a user who picked one could never return to the
      automatic pick. Rendered ONLY when a cover is actually stored, which is what keeps the two
      controls from being ambiguous in the common case: with nothing chosen there is just the
      chooser.

      IF BOTH ARE USED IN ONE SUBMIT, CLEARING WINS — see ProjectsController#project_params. That is
      stated rather than left to be discovered, because it is the one combination whose outcome the
      form cannot show.
    %>
    <% if chosen %>
      <label class="field-inline muted">
        <%= check_box_tag "project[cover_clear]", "1", false %>
        Clear it and go back to picking automatically
      </label>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%#
    THE SWEEP'S OWN SWITCH (stage 4, S4-2; story 4.3). A checkbox, so `f.check_box` emits the
    hidden "0" field that makes unchecking reach the controller at all — without it an unchecked
    box sends nothing and the attribute never changes.
    NOT A "don't touch my files" MASTER SWITCH: uploads, the addon save door and Move all still
    write where you tell them. This is only the automatic sort of the folder's own root.
  %>
  <label class="field-inline">
    <%= f.check_box :autofile %>
    File loose files into subfolders automatically
    <span class="field-hint muted">Off, the app still lists and links this folder's files — it
      just leaves them where you put them.</span>
  </label>

  <div class="form-actions">
    <%= f.submit(project.persisted? ? "Save changes" : "Create project", class: "btn primary") %>
    <%= link_to "Cancel", (project.persisted? ? project_path(project) : projects_path), class: "linkbtn" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
